    Match tasks by email, handle sg_assigned_to as a string, drop committed key
    
    Task ownership now resolves the current user by email address (HumanUser.email)
    rather than login, deriving <os-login>@5and8.ai and honouring SGDESK_USER_EMAIL
    and SGDESK_EMAIL_DOMAIN overrides. Both SGDESK_USER and SGDESK_USER_EMAIL are
    injected into launched DCCs.
    
    sg_assigned_to turned out to be a plain String field on this site, not an entity
    link -- filtering with an entity dict fails with "expected [String, NilClass]
    data type(s) but got Hash". my_tasks() now branches on TASK_OWNER_IS_ENTITY and
    compares the string directly; resolve_owner() supplies the value to match and
    falls back to the email address when no HumanUser matches.
    
    The ShotGrid script key is no longer defaulted in config.py. SGClient now fails
    with a clear message when SG_SCRIPT_KEY is unset. The key that was previously
    committed must be rotated -- it remains readable in this repository history.
    
    Also adds HANDOFF.md and DEPLOY-ROCKY9.md, a .gitignore, and untracks
    __pycache__ and .idea.
    
